 "degrade_seed": 11,
 "rule_text": "ROBUSTNESS TEST (DESIGN \u00a76.5 'Robustness test'; reporting level 3 = exploratory; NO adoption decision depends on it). Model fixed: GBDT_AB_17 on feature set A+B (tb_asym_* excluded), hyper-parameters fixed, no re-tuning, seeds config/seeds.yaml, same dev folds as the incumbent. Degraded proteomes (scripts/robustness/degrade_proteome.py, seed 11 = seeds[0]): fragments (20% of proteins truncated to a random 50-80% of their length at a random N- or C-terminus), split (5% of genes split at a random internal point; longer piece keeps the gene ID, shorter gets a new ID), fused (2% of genes get another random non-labelled gene's sequence appended; donor removed), missing (15% of genes removed), haplotig (5% of genes get an extra near-identical copy, 1% random substitutions, new ID), combined (all of them: missing -> fused -> split -> fragments -> haplotig). Yeast: all six kinds (+ an identity control = natural proteome through the same route); human: combined only. Tier A+B features of each degraded proteome from `slparalog predict --features-only --tier-b` (existing panel databases; <=8 threads; runtime recorded). Evaluation (thinning N->T design): train on the NATURAL features of the training folds, evaluate the held-out fold on the DEGRADED features of the same labelled pairs; pairs map to degraded gene IDs through the mapping table; pairs that lose a gene or are no longer called are scored at the minimum score (one tie block), B1 (ident_global) identically; the population (natural labelled & called dev pairs) is unchanged. Reported per species x kind: per-fold mean AP of the model and of B1, natural and degraded, dAP vs B1 per species (T_pf for the combined kind, where both species exist), and the natural-to-degraded drops (model, B1, model-minus-B1) with 95% stratified group-bootstrap percentile CIs (same resamples, paired); pooled-OOF APs, prevalence and counts, and the number of lost pairs. No decision rule: no thresholds, nothing is adopted or rejected on this result.",
